	"barks": {
		"day": ["Fog's lifting. Should be clear by noon. It won't be.", "Lanterns stay lit by day here. Don't laugh. Don't ask.", "Tide's out. The strand's full of things the sea gave back.",
			"Keep inside the lantern line. That's all I'll say.", "The bell's quiet. That's a good sign, here.", "Gulls won't come near the bay. Never have.",
			"Herring at the stalls today. Thin ones. Better than none.", "Saw the sun for a whole minute this morning. Lovely, it was.",
			"Grey sea, grey sky, grey fog. You get used to it. You don't.", "A pirate ship? Hope they've brought oil to sell.",
			"Smoke from the smokehouse. Eel again, then.", "Mind the dead trees. They drop limbs without warning.",
			"Can't see the wreck from here today. Good.", "Somebody's whistling on the strand. Stop them. Please.",
			"The fog's thinner up by the graveyard. Funny, that.", "Salt on the doorstep fresh this morning. Did you do yours?",
			"Nobody fishes near the wreck. Nobody with any sense.", "Wet everything. My bread's wet. My bones are wet.",
			"The chapel's door is always open. In case you need running to."],
		"evening": ["Dusk. Lamp oil, everyone. Fill them high.", "Bell's going to ring the hours soon. Count them.", "Light goes all at once here. One moment grey, then black.",
			"Children in. Shutters shut. Lamps in the windows.", "Fog's coming off the bay. See it? Like breath.",
			"Inn's warm and the fire's high. Best place to be when the dark comes.", "Somebody check the lamps on the strand. The far ones.",
