			"Supper's eel pie. Again.", "The dead trees creak more at dusk. Wind, they say.", "Bar the door. Then check you've barred it.",
			"Salt on the sill. Lamp in the window. Prayer on your lips.", "Watch the waterline. Things come up with the tide.",
			"Lamplighter's late. Somebody go and see.", "Nobody walks alone after the bell. Pair up.",
			"Cold coming in with the fog. Wear the thick coat.", "Mist's in the graveyard already. It always goes there first.",
			"Last boat's in. Count the crew. Count them again."],
		"night": ["Keep to the light. Whatever calls you out of it.", "Shh. Footsteps on the strand. Wet ones.", "Don't answer if they knock. They know your name. That's not a reason.",
			"The fog's at the lantern line, leaning. Feel it?", "Ghost-light out by the dead trees. Don't follow it.", "Somebody's singing in the bay. Nobody's in the bay.",
			"Bell from the wreck again. Three rings. Three.", "Lamp's guttering. Oil, quick, before it goes.", "Cold spot by the well. Walk round it.",
			"Night watch. I've seen things, captain. I've stopped telling people.", "The dead don't like the bell. Ring it if they come close.",
			"Wet footprints on the chapel step. Leading in.", "Don't look at the water too long. It looks back.", "Moon's up. Fog's silver. Pretty, if you don't think about it.",
			"Who's out at this hour? Oh. A pirate. Have a lantern. Have two.", "Drowned men walk slow. Run, and you'll be fine. Mostly.",
			"Lamp's lit, salt's down, door's barred. Now we wait for morning.", "Something tapped my window. Third floor. I live on the third floor.",
			"Late for the living. Early for the rest."],
		"nets": ["Hand me the twine. The tarred one.", "Something tore this in the night. Look at the edges. Clean.", "Herring, two crabs and a boot. A boot with a foot in it. Throw it back.",
			"Knots for nets, knots for nooses. Don't ask me which I'm better at.", "Nets come up heavy near the wreck. We don't set them there.",
			"Mend it before the tide, or the tide mends it for you.", "Found a ring in the net. Gave it back. You do."],
		"forage": ["Past the lanterns already? Brave. Daft, but brave.", "Mushrooms under the dead oaks. Pale ones. Don't eat them.", "Wolf tracks. Or something with a wolf's feet.",
			"Bones in the bracken. Old ones, I hope.", "Fog's thicker out here. Keep a lamp close.", "Moss on everything. Even me, if I stand still long enough.",
			"Shh. Somebody's crying in the wood. There's nobody in the wood."],
		"dock": ["Tie up tight. The tide pulls hard here, and it pulls things off decks.", "Ship from the mainland? Not for a month. They don't like coming.",
			"Your ship? Keep a lamp at her stern tonight. Trust me.", "Pass the wreck to port on the way out. Never to starboard. Never.",
			"Mooring posts are rotten. That one's the least rotten.", "Grey sea today. Grey every day.", "Fog came down so fast last week a boat sailed past the landing. Never found it."],
		"boats": ["Every boat here's got a lamp at the bow. Every one.", "Caulk the seams, tar the hull, salt the deck.", "Beached her for the winter. The sea's no friend in winter.",
